-- UIC voluntary motor vehicle insurance rules, Part 1, Part II: Article 4 (UIC's rights
-- and duties), Article 5 (the policyholder's rights and duties), and the duty to refund in
-- Article 3.2. Quotations (`src:N`) are generated from line N of
-- ../../source/raw/uic-autojoy.txt.
--
-- THE CLOCK. Every period in these articles is stated in "ngày" (days), and the document
-- never says calendar or working days: they are read as calendar days (fork F11). A
-- regulative rule here counts from day 0, the day of the event that starts it (the notice
-- received, the change, the loss), and `WITHIN n` is met by an act on day n (fork F12).
--
-- WHAT IS NOT A REGULATIVE RULE HERE. The rights in Art 4.1 and 5.1 and the duties with no
-- time and no consequence (Art 4.2.1, 4.2.2, 4.2.6, 4.2.8, 5.2.2, 5.2.3, 5.2.5, 5.2.9, 5.2.11)
-- are quoted and marked inert. The duties to notify "immediately" (Art 5.2.6.1, 5.2.10)
-- carry no number of days; whether a notice was immediate is a fact
-- (`not notifying the UIC hotline immediately`, ...), and Article 15 attaches the
-- consequence (uic-autojoy-p1-settlement.l4). Paying the premium (Art 5.2.1) is enforced by
-- Art 3.1 and 16.1, declaring honestly (5.2.2) by Art 15.1.5.1, honesty in the claim (5.2.7)
-- by Art 11.18, and the third-party rights (5.2.8) by Art 15.1.3.

